 "build_recommendation": {
  "decision": "Keep action.rs. Do not replace it with a learned representation now.",
  "optional_small_build": "rrr-first without BPE as a fallback labeller for commands action.rs labels `other` and as a learned env-class signal: shell-syntax lex -> ~17 sparse positional features (hash map, ~1.1k vocab) -> sum rows of W (1.1k x 32 f32, ~140 KB; 35 KB int8) -> L2 normalise -> nearest of ~20-30 prototypes (32-d) if cos >= tau else new class. ~1.3k FLOPs/command: a few microseconds in Rust (Python: 0.34 ms lex+features, 0.14 ms project, 1.4 us nearest). Fitted offline at condition time by reduced-rank ridge regression from command features to FIRST-IN-SESSION outcome features.",
  "expected_value": "~0 calls and ~0% of $ on repositories action.rs covers; on repositories with unknown tools at most the recovery ceiling (<= 2.5 calls/session, ~8% of calls), realistically a fraction (LORO gold agreement 0.44-0.60).",
  "gate": "Before any build: live micro-slice (~$5, harness protocol) of the learned `pip install -e .` reflex on marshmallow/attrs; drop the learned route if p_follow < 0.6 or local saving < 50% of replay.",
  "transferable_finding": "Condition outcome-based learning on 'before any repair' (first-in-session outcomes): it recovers state-independent action properties (the .venv/system split) with no hand-written features."
 },
